# The Go services' images are built with the whole repo as their "build
# context": the files Docker can see while it builds. This file says which
# files are sent to Docker. "*" leaves everything out, and each "!" line
# lets one folder back in. So secrets (.env), node_modules and .git never
# reach an image, and builds start faster.
# Learn more: docs/learn/docker.md#the-build-context
*
!packages/go
!services
